## findings

### Direct answers to the six questions

| Question | Verdict |
|---|---|
| Two-op handle + request-field guard ⇒ trace is the only context? | **No.** Defeated by ordinary Python attribute access (P0-1). |
| Handshake identity from a probe invocation? | **Not acceptable as primary.** SMP1 §2 derives it per-connection from the server hello, which the trial receives and discards (P1-4). |
| Ten trace-derived metrics correct? `context_bytes` right? | **No** on four of ten; `context_bytes` scope is wrong and biases the arm under test (P0-2, P1-6/7/12). |
| Reusing S20-610 `offline_injected` / `forbidden` honest? | **No** — S20-620 rescopes a frozen shared control by prose (P0-3). |
